---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../../../components/StatusBadge.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="LEAPMOTOR A10 Urban Departure | Small Car, Solved"
  description="A city-focused LEAPMOTOR A10 concept for commuting, errands and short weekend trips, with clear fitment and market boundaries."
  image="/images/a10/city-departure.webp"
  alternatePath="/solutions/a10-city-departure/"
>
  <SiteHeader slot="header" lang="en" />
  <article class="article-shell">
    <a class="article-back" href="/en/">← Back to home</a>
    <header class="article-head">
      <StatusBadge status="concept" lang="en" />
      <h1>LEAPMOTOR A10 Urban Departure: define the whole character first</h1>
      <p class="article-summary">A concept for commuting, errands and short weekend trips—followed by separate checks for product fitment, dimensions, installation and safety.</p>
      <p class="article-status-note"><strong>Current status:</strong> Concept. This page communicates design direction; it does not claim confirmed product fitment or a completed vehicle installation.</p>
    </header>

    <img class="article-hero" src="/images/a10/city-departure.webp" alt="LEAPMOTOR A10 urban-life concept parked on a city street" width="1200" height="1600" />

    <div class="article-body">
      <h2>What this proposal is designed to solve</h2>
      <p>Many modification projects begin with a shopping list. The result can be more accessories without a more coherent car. This proposal starts with the life around the vehicle and adds only the changes that support it.</p>
      <p>The use case is deliberately specific: city commuting, everyday errands and short weekend trips. The goal is not to make a compact car imitate an off-roader, but to keep its approachable proportions while improving visual order and everyday usefulness.</p>

      <h2>Why subtraction comes first</h2>
      <p>Before choosing products, the proposal asks four practical questions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Which parts of the original colour and proportion are already worth keeping?</li>
        <li>Does an added item solve a real use case or only work in a photograph?</li>
        <li>Will cleaning, loading, clearance or daily maintenance become harder?</li>
        <li>Are product fitment, dimensions and mounting methods supported by reliable information?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Until those questions are answered, the visual remains a concept rather than a buying list.</p>

      <h2>Design direction</h2>
      <p>The concept keeps the A10 compact and city-friendly, with three priorities:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A controlled colour hierarchy.</strong> The body remains the visual anchor; accessories do not compete through unrelated colours.</li>
        <li><strong>Accessories with a purpose.</strong> Roof and loading elements illustrate a short-trip use case and are not presented as confirmed fitment.</li>
        <li><strong>One system, not isolated products.</strong> Wheels, exterior parts, storage and cabin gear should support the same lifestyle brief.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>International-market boundaries</h2>
      <p>The LEAPMOTOR A10 serves international markets as well as its home market, but model naming, trim availability, accessory supply and road regulations can differ by country. Readers should treat this page as a shared design direction, not a universal product-fitment claim.</p>
      <p>At concept stage, this page does not confirm specific brands, mounting dimensions, load limits, effects on range or wind noise, or legal suitability in any particular jurisdiction.</p>

      <h2>From concept to installation</h2>
      <p>A customer-ready installation reference requires four additional stages:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Check real products, vehicle information and market-specific requirements.</li>
        <li>Measure key vehicle locations and remove incompatible options.</li>
        <li>Document mounting methods, actual cost and installation issues.</li>
        <li>Review the result after continued use and record what was kept, changed or removed.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>For overseas-market information, product fitment data or collaboration enquiries, contact <a href="mailto:xiaocheyoujie@proton.me">xiaocheyoujie@proton.me</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <SiteFooter slot="footer" lang="en" />
</BaseLayout>
